# Point the frontend at the MAGI TEST DEPLOY.
#
#   npm run dev -- --mode magi
#
# Deliberately NOT .env: setting VITE_CONTRACT_ID flips the app into WALLET
# MODE (see chain.svelte.ts), which disables the dev-chain name-only sign-in and
# requires a real Hive wallet for every action. Keeping it behind an explicit
# --mode means the default `./build.sh web` still runs against the local
# simulator, which is where day-to-day work belongs.
#
# ⚠️ THIS IS A THROWAWAY TEST CONTRACT — #10, THE TOKEN LEDGER
# (vsc1BiHbDTG…1ZG, code bafkreihztepfwl5noydp3qab7odgsfvtfetupozxytbxw4uorxqdm5nrsu,
# genesis 109,681,561, deployed 2026-09-06) from @lassecashmagi.
#
# It runs the MAINNET CLOCK, not TESTWINDOWS — a day is a day here. It carries
# the standard-token ledger: balances live in a real magi_token
# (vsc1Bq7L9VhLbN6eJdCD8My9jmjAdpxADJLEGR) that this core OWNS, proven on chain
# by @lassecashmagi being refused with "Must be owner to mint". Its code CID is
# byte-identical to contract/artifacts/main-tokenledger.wasm — the exact
# artifact that goes to production — so what you exercise here is what ships.
#
# Its owner key still exists. NEVER point real users at it, and never put this
# id anywhere near lassecash.com's Cloudflare environment.
VITE_CONTRACT_ID=vsc1BiHbDTG9ppYUfEwXqLzCCkzS7MjGHFp1ZG
VITE_MAGI_NET_ID=vsc-mainnet
VITE_CHAIN_URL=https://api.vsc.eco/api/v1/graphql
# NO VITE_TESTWINDOWS: throwaway #10 runs the mainnet clock, so a day is a day.
# Setting it here would divide every duration on the page by 240.

# Pre-launch: only /check and /about are reachable (see src/routes/+layout.ts).
# DELETE THIS LINE at genesis, together with VITE_TESTWINDOWS.
# TEMPORARILY DISABLED for local throwaway-#6 wallet testing — re-enable
# (uncomment) before this file is ever used against anything but a throwaway.
# VITE_PRELAUNCH=1
